  "id": "airfreightforwarding",
  "neon": "#ffb43a",
  "note": "AIRFREIGHT FORWARDING — the air-cargo forwarder on Kessler Street.\n\nThe tile's prose: a low prefab office ringed by roller-shuttered bays, the airfield aprons close\nenough that jet-wash rattles the signs. Clipboards, barcode guns and a coffee urn that never cools.\n\nSo the front is a lit office strip of prefab panels with a band of windows and a door, standing\nforward of a taller shed that carries a roller bay on each flank and the back. The name is on the\noffice fascia and FREIGHT goes on a board on the shed above it, so the second sign says the trade\nrather than the name again. A windsock on the shed roof is for the airfield next door.",
